<ContentPage title="Security & Trust" eyebrow="Security before evidence" intro="Start with context, not confidential files. Protected information belongs behind a controlled classification, processing and human-review decision.">
<section class="content-section"><div class="shell security-panel"><div class="security-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Stage 1</div><h2>High-level context only.</h2><p>Do not provide incident files, personal information, credentials, restricted contracts, evidence packs, system exports or detailed cyber architecture through the public website.</p></div><div class="security-detail"><div class="boundary"><div class="boundary-zone"><h3>PUBLIC</h3><ul><li>Business challenge</li><li>Industry and operating context</li><li>Jurisdiction</li><li>Desired outcome and timing</li><li>Business contact information</li></ul></div><div class="boundary-gate"><span>Human-controlled gate</span></div><div class="boundary-zone"><h3>CONTROLLED LATER</h3><ul><li>Documents and evidence</li><li>Restricted operational data</li><li>Detailed security information</li><li>Assessment material</li><li>Protected records</li></ul></div></div><div class="human-note"><strong>SAI advises. Humans decide.</strong> Consequential judgement remains with authorised people. Technology does not certify compliance, accept risk or replace professional accountability.</div></div></div></section>
</ContentPage>
